content/browser/accessibility: guard CloseDir with the /proc scan on BSD.

Origin: EmberBSD (AI-assisted), not submitted upstream.
Source: Chromium electron-source tree under EmberBSD.
DiscoverOrca() is NOTIMPLEMENTED on IS_BSD, so the only caller of the
anonymous CloseDir() deleter is compiled out and Clang reports
-Werror,-Wunused-function. Define the helper only where /proc is scanned
instead of silencing the diagnostic.

--- a/content/browser/accessibility/browser_accessibility_state_impl_auralinux.cc	2026-10-28 09:32:14.298752154 +0300
+++ b/content/browser/accessibility/browser_accessibility_state_impl_auralinux.cc	2026-10-28 09:32:14.317254490 +0300
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 
 namespace content {
 
+#if !BUILDFLAG(IS_BSD)
 namespace {
 
 // Custom deleter function for DIR* that calls closedir
@@ -34,6 +35,7 @@
 }
 
 }  // namespace
+#endif  // !BUILDFLAG(IS_BSD)
 
 namespace internal {
 
